claimed: okay-script-https-default -- operator ask 2026-09-07: HTTPS out of the box, with a proxy and without, minimally. Four things and no more. (1) okay-tls gains Tls.selfSigned(keystore, host): Either[String, SSLContext] -- a PKCS12 generated ONCE with the JDK's own keytool (openssl as the fallback, a named refusal when neither is there), reused on restart, fingerprint printed; OKAY_TLS=self serves https with zero setup. (2) Site(hsts: Option[Int]) adds Strict-Transport-Security on SECURE responses only, off by default because HSTS on a self-signed dev host pins a browser against you; OKAY_HSTS=<seconds>. (3) Site(httpsOnly) answers a request the container sees as insecure with a 301 to the same URL on https (the Host header's authority) -- behind a proxy that is the http->https redirect, with own TLS it is the plaintext port's job; OKAY_HTTPS_ONLY=1. (4) OKAY_HTTP_PORT=<n>: when serving TLS, also bind a plaintext port that ONLY redirects. Touches okay-tls, Site.scala, Serve.scala, specs/okay-script.md + specs/tls.md, the guide; Live tests for the self-signed handshake and the redirect port.
